      <div class="rd-inner">
        <div class="rd-eyebrow">Coaching &amp; Supervision</div>
        <h1 class="rd-h2">Frequently asked questions</h1>
        <div class="rd-faq-grid">
          <div class="rd-faq-list">
            <div class="rd-faq-item is-active">
              <button class="rd-faq-q" aria-expanded="true"><span class="rd-num">01</span><span class="rd-q">How do coaching, supervision and therapy differ?</span><span class="faq-toggle"></span></button>
              <div class="rd-faq-a"><div class="rd-faq-a-inner"><p>Coaching is about professional or personal goals, decisions and roles, for example a new leadership role, a career reorientation, questions about parenting, or coping with stress at work.</p><p>Supervision looks at your professional practice: your work with clients, collaboration within the team and the structures of your organization. Therapy and counseling start where emotional distress, crises or relationship issues are in the foreground.</p><p>The boundaries are fluid. In our first session, we clarify together which framework fits your concern.</p></div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="rd-faq-item">
              <button class="rd-faq-q" aria-expanded="false"><span class="rd-num">02</span><span class="rd-q">What concerns can I bring to coaching?</span><span class="faq-toggle"></span></button>
              <div class="rd-faq-a"><div class="rd-faq-a-inner"><ul class="rd-faq-ul"><li><strong>Role and leadership:</strong> taking on a leadership role or changes in your own role</li><li><strong>Orientation:</strong> professional reorientation and upcoming decisions</li><li><strong>Conflicts:</strong> tensions within the team or with supervisors</li><li><strong>Strain:</strong> dealing with pressure, stress and looming exhaustion</li><li><strong>Parent coaching:</strong> questions about parenting, the parental role and family life</li><li><strong>Couples coaching:</strong> shared life and career planning, reconciling family and work</li></ul><p>If you are unsure whether your concern is a good fit, we can talk about it in our first session.</p></div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="rd-faq-item">
              <button class="rd-faq-q" aria-expanded="false"><span class="rd-num">03</span><span class="rd-q">Which forms of supervision do you offer?</span><span class="faq-toggle"></span></button>
              <div class="rd-faq-a"><div class="rd-faq-a-inner"><ul class="rd-faq-ul"><li><strong>Individual supervision</strong> for professionals in social, educational, therapeutic and medical fields as well as for people with leadership responsibility</li><li><strong>Team supervision</strong> on collaboration, communication and role clarification within the team</li><li><strong>Group supervision</strong> for professional exchange and reflection on work with clients</li></ul><p>In every format, the content can focus on case supervision, leadership supervision or collaboration in the team.</p></div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="rd-faq-item">
              <button class="rd-faq-q" aria-expanded="false"><span class="rd-num">04</span><span class="rd-q">How does working together begin?</span><span class="faq-toggle"></span></button>
              <div class="rd-faq-a"><div class="rd-faq-a-inner"><p>It begins with a non-binding, free initial contact by phone or online by video. In about 20 minutes, we get to know each other and clarify the framework.</p><p>This is followed by the in-depth first session. We clarify your concerns and whether it feels right to begin working together. The first session is a regular session and is charged at the usual rates.</p><p>If an organization commissions the coaching or supervision, I hold a scoping meeting with those responsible after initial contact. In it, we clarify the occasion, goals, scope and framework.</p></div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="rd-faq-item">
              <button class="rd-faq-q" aria-expanded="false"><span class="rd-num">05</span><span class="rd-q">How long does a session last, and how far apart are appointments?</span><span class="faq-toggle"></span></button>
              <div class="rd-faq-a"><div class="rd-faq-a-inner"><div class="faq-facts">
                  <div class="faq-fact"><span>Individual</span><strong>from 60 min.</strong></div>
                  <div class="faq-fact"><span>Two or more people</span><strong>from 90 min.</strong></div>
                  <div class="faq-fact"><span>Coaching</span><strong>2–4 weeks</strong></div>
                  <div class="faq-fact"><span>Supervision</span><strong>often monthly</strong></div>
                </div>
                <p>I offer individual sessions of 60 minutes or longer, and if needed 90 or 120 minutes. Couples coaching and sessions with several people usually last at least 90 minutes.</p><p>Coaching usually consists of a few sessions spaced 2 to 4 weeks apart. Supervision often takes place on an ongoing basis, for example once a month. We set the rhythm together and adjust it as needed along the way.</p></div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="rd-faq-item">
              <button class="rd-faq-q" aria-expanded="false"><span class="rd-num">06</span><span class="rd-q">Do coaching and supervision take place online or on site?</span><span class="faq-toggle"></span></button>
              <div class="rd-faq-a"><div class="rd-faq-a-inner"><p>Sessions take place in Berlin-Moabit (INSA-Berlin · Alt-Moabit 91b) or online by video. I also conduct group and team supervision on site at your organization's location.</p></div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="rd-faq-item">
              <button class="rd-faq-q" aria-expanded="false"><span class="rd-num">07</span><span class="rd-q">Is the content treated confidentially, even if my organization pays the costs?</span><span class="faq-toggle"></span></button>
              <div class="rd-faq-a"><div class="rd-faq-a-inner"><p>Yes. In principle, the content of the sessions remains confidential, even if your organization commissions the work. As part of clarifying the assignment, the participants agree transparently which information is passed on, and in what form, to management or the HR department.</p><p>For quality assurance, I take part in supervision of my own work. I always bring in content anonymized there.</p></div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="rd-faq-item">
              <button class="rd-faq-q" aria-expanded="false"><span class="rd-num">08</span><span class="rd-q">What costs can I expect?</span><span class="faq-toggle"></span></button>
              <div class="rd-faq-a"><div class="rd-faq-a-inner"><p>If you pay as a private individual, the hourly rate is 150 euros. For organizations, I agree the fee individually and prepare a written offer.</p><a class="rd-faq-link" href="{{ '/en/coaching-supervision/kosten/' | url }}">All details on costs, invoicing and cancellation<span class="rd-chev"></span></a></div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="rd-faq-item">
              <button class="rd-faq-q" aria-expanded="false"><span class="rd-num">09</span><span class="rd-q">What qualifications do you have for coaching and supervision?</span><span class="faq-toggle"></span></button>
              <div class="rd-faq-a"><div class="rd-faq-a-inner"><p>My services are based on my qualifications from recognized further training in coaching (DGSv) and supervision (DGSv/SG) as well as in Systemic Therapy &amp; Counseling (DGSF).</p></div></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="rd-faq-detail" aria-live="polite"><div class="rd-faq-detail-bar"></div><div class="rd-faq-detail-body"></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

